claude-youtube-editor — https://github.com/hassancs91/claude-youtube-editor
MIT License, Copyright (c) Hassan

Adapted:
  * The plan-then-tool shape used throughout post-production: a declarative JSON
    plan is the source of truth, a tool consumes it, a shared library grows, and
    a hard user-audit gate stands before anything is rendered or mixed.
  * SFX method — library-first sourcing, the per-cue plan schema, the sidechain
    duck under voice, and the measured gain calibration: long-form -12..-18 dB,
    short-form corrections, and the +3..+5 dB transient correction that exists
    because percussive clips hit the -1.5 dBFS peak ceiling before reaching the
    -20 LUFS loudness target.
  * The RMS audibility check and its pitfalls: the >= +4 dB threshold for a
    story-critical cue, the ~0.3s window for transients, measuring a riser at its
    final third, and the finding that a cue sitting fully under continuous speech
    never measures at any gain.
  * Remotion shot authoring rules that keep a render from crashing: frame-based
    animation only, strictly monotonic interpolate ranges, Easing.bezier called
    directly, no useState/useEffect/setTimeout.
  * ffmpeg assembly discipline: the A/V duration equality gate, and re-stamping
    constant frame rate by placing -r before -i.
  * ElevenLabs text-to-speech prosody stitching across consecutive requests.
  * AssemblyAI as the transcription provider, and the idea of biasing the
    recognizer with per-video keyterms.
  * capture_web — the step-runner shape for driving a browser against a spec file
    (goto/click/fill/wait/scroll/shot), minus its `eval` step (arbitrary JS from a
    spec file is a credential-injection risk this plugin refuses to carry) and
    minus its VS Code serve-web integration (not relevant to a promo pipeline).
    Reworked as `tools/gen_app_screen.py capture`.
  * screencast, browser and kit Remotion components (`remotion/src/lib/{screencast,
    browser,kit}.tsx`) — cursor/click keyframes as viewport fractions, cut-vs-
    crossfade transition rules, browser chrome. Ported into
    `templates/remotion/lib/` with every Claude-Code-specific piece and the
    `lucide-react` dependency removed; brand tokens come from this plugin's own
    `brand.json`, not a shipped palette.
  * gen-registry, render-all and qa-frames scripts (`remotion/scripts/`) — the
    composition-discovery-then-render shape and the QA-still convention (a still
    at every named cue, read rather than trusted). Ported with the `--type` /
    typeOfGroup grouping removed (this plugin has no shot-type taxonomy to group
    by).
  * verify_cut method — a second ASR pass over the finished render, diffed
    against the intended script text with `difflib`, reporting inserted/missing/
    replaced words, intra-sentence gaps, low-confidence tokens and per-scene
    drift. Reworked as `tools/verify_render.py` and validator check P6, sharing
    the AssemblyAI client already factored out of `gen_subs.py` rather than
    copying it.
  * make_stems method — full-length, ungated WAV stems per layer (voice/SFX/
    music) for a human editor, gains baked in instead of the mix-time ducking the
    finished master uses. Reworked as `tools/make_stems.py`.
  * gen_music method — library-first track generation against ElevenLabs Music
    (skip a mood that already has a track, `--force` to regenerate) with
    loudness normalisation toward a target LUFS clamped by a peak ceiling.
    Reworked as `tools/gen_music.py` against this plugin's own mood palette.
  * clean_voice methods — ElevenLabs Voice Isolator and ffmpeg `arnndn` (RNNoise)
    as two interchangeable noise-reduction paths, RMS level matched back to the
    source, and the refuse-rather-than-stretch duration gate the Voice Changer
    already enforces. Reworked as `tools/clean_voice.py`; the three RNNoise
    models (`sh.rnnn`, `cb.rnnn`, `bd.rnnn`) are copied verbatim into
    `tools/models/rnnoise/` — the one sanctioned binary asset in this repo.
  * bake.py split/insert filter method — frame-accurate three-segment concat for
    inserting a full clip into a master, and a crop-into-a-box-plus-overlay
    filter graph for picture-in-picture. Reworked as `composite.py split` and
    `composite.py insert`, both running through this plugin's existing A/V
    duration gate.
  * composite_logo.py and thumb_scrim.py — deterministic thumbnail post-process
    (real logo pasted with its own colours, headline scrim darkened until a
    measured WCAG contrast target is reached). Ported minus every Claude brand
    colour default and the tile/mark options that assumed a specific logo mark;
    the logo and its colours always come from the user's own file.
  * yt_stats.py — OAuth installed-app flow against the YouTube Data and
    Analytics APIs, read-only scopes, writing views/watch-time/retention into a
    project's packaging calibration file. Ported as-is; the token and client
    secret live under the user's home directory, never in this repo.

Not adopted from claude-youtube-editor (v3.1.0 pass): gen_video.py (fal — this plugin
renders through the indusia MCP servers only), gen_avatar.mjs (this plugin's proven
lip-sync path is VEO native lip-sync plus the ElevenLabs Voice Changer, not a
separate avatar generator), the clean-cut family (render_cuts, cutlib, analyze_cut,
make_proxy, make_review, format_transcript, editor/ — built for editing a long-form
recording, not a short assembled promo), brand-setup, yt_upload.py, notion_sync.py
(brand values already come from strategic-brief.md; upload/sync sit outside what a
video-production plugin should own), lib/vscode.tsx (Claude-Code-specific), and
gen_thumbnail.py (thumbnail rendering is the image plugin's job — this plugin only
adds the deterministic logo/scrim post-process on top of it).

